    <p style="color: #94a3b8; font-size: 0.88rem; line-height: 1.65; margin: 0;">A certificate issued by a recognized insurer, covering the bike for the entire transit period. It should detail the coverage limits, policy number, and contact details of the insurer.</p>
  </div>
  <div style="background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.75); border: 1.5px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08); border-radius: 14px; padding: 24px 20px; box-shadow: 0 10px 25px rgba(0,0,0,0.35); transition: transform 0.2s ease, border-color 0.2s ease;">
    <div style="display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; width: 42px; height: 42px; border-radius: 10px; background: #a855f722; color: #a855f7; font-weight: 800; font-size: 1.05rem; margin-bottom: 14px;">04</div>
    <h3 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.1rem; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 10px; line-height: 1.4;">IBA‑Approved Consignment Bilty:</h3>
    <p style="color: #94a3b8; font-size: 0.88rem; line-height: 1.65; margin: 0;">A bilty issued by the International Bilty Association (IBA) that records the consignor, consignee, carrier, and freight terms. It serves as the official contract of carriage and is required for all sea freight movements.</p>
  </div>
</div>

<p style="font-size: 1.04rem; line-height: 1.75; color: #f1f5f9; font-weight: 500; margin-bottom: 12px;">Special emphasis must be placed on the <strong>100% declared‑value marine transit insurance</strong>.</p>
<ul style="list-style: none; padding-left: 0; margin: 16px 0 20px 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 10px;"><li style="display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.03); border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.07); padding: 10px 14px; border-radius: 8px; font-size: 0.92rem; line-height: 1.55; color: #cbd5e1;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 4px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.9rem;"></i><span>This type of insurance ensures that the full market value of the bike is insured against loss, damage, or theft during sea transport.</span></li><li style="display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.03); border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.07); padding: 10px 14px; border-radius: 8px; font-size: 0.92rem; line-height: 1.55; color: #cbd5e1;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 4px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.9rem;"></i><span>Unlike standard policies that offer a fixed sum, 100% declared‑value coverage recalculates the insured amount based on the bike’s actual value at the time of shipment, providing comprehensive protection.</span></li></ul>
<p style="font-size: 1.04rem; line-height: 1.75; color: #f1f5f9; font-weight: 500; margin-bottom: 12px;">Insurers typically require a recent appraisal or purchase invoice to substantiate the declared value, so be sure to have these documents ready.</p>
<ul style="list-style: none; padding-left: 0; margin: 16px 0 20px 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 10px;"><li style="display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.03); border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.07); padding: 10px 14px; border-radius: 8px; font-size: 0.92rem; line-height: 1.55; color: #cbd5e1;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 4px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.9rem;"></i><span>When you present the bilty and insurance certificate to the shipping line, the 100% declared‑value clause will be highlighted, guaranteeing that any claim will be settled at the bike’s full value, thereby eliminating the risk of under‑insurance.</span></li></ul>

<p>By meticulously compiling these documents and confirming the 100% declared‑value coverage, you can confidently entrust your bike’s journey to Varkala’s marine transport network, knowing that all legal and financial safeguards are in place.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>


<section class="content-ui-section" style="padding: 55px 0; background: #0b132b; color: #cbd5e1; border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.07);">
  <div class="container" style="max-width: 1060px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 0 15px;">
    <div style="background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.65); border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08); border-radius: 16px; padding: 36px 32px; box-shadow: 0 12px 30px rgba(0,0,0,0.35);">
      <span style="background: rgba(245, 158, 11, 0.12); color: #f59e0b; border: 1px solid rgba(245, 158, 11, 0.35); padding: 4px 14px; border-radius: 20px; font-size: 0.78rem; font-weight: 700; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.5px; display: inline-block; margin-bottom: 14px;">HANDOVER INSPECTION</span>
      <h2 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.7rem; font-weight: 800; line-height: 1.35; margin-bottom: 18px;">Destination Handover, Odometer Sign-Off &amp; Joint Condition Inspection for Bike Transportation In Varkala</h2>
      <div style="font-size: 1.02rem; line-height: 1.8; color: #cbd5e1;"><p style="font-size: 1.04rem; line-height: 1.75; color: #f1f5f9; font-weight: 500; margin-bottom: 12px;">When a two‑wheeler or motorcycle is delivered to its destination, a strict handover protocol guarantees that the vehicle’s condition, mileage, and ownership documentation are all accurate and verified.</p>
<ul style="list-style: none; padding-left: 0; margin: 16px 0 20px 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 10px;"><li style="display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.03); border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.07); padding: 10px 14px; border-radius: 8px; font-size: 0.92rem; line-height: 1.55; color: #cbd5e1;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 4px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.9rem;"></i><span>The process is designed to be performed under daylight, enabling a clear visual comparison with the original pickup photos and to ensure the odometer reading matches the logistics record (LR) bilty.</span></li></ul>
<p>Each step is documented and signed off by the delivery agent and the recipient.</p>

<ul>
  <li><strong>Daylight Condition Re‑Inspection</strong>
    <ul>
      <li>Position the vehicle in a well‑lit area, ensuring all panels, wheels, and accessories are fully visible.</li>
      <li>Open the original pickup photo archive (digital or physical) and compare the current state of the motorcycle with each image.</li>
      <li>Mark any discrepancies—scratches, dents, or missing parts—using a color‑coded marker and photograph the affected areas.</li>
      <li>Confirm that the lighting conditions match those of the pickup photos to avoid misinterpretation of paint or component status.</li>
    </ul>
  </li>

  <li><strong>Odometer Verification Against LR Bilty</strong>
    <ul>
      <li>Locate the vehicle’s odometer and read the mileage, noting any irregularities or inconsistencies.</li>
      <li>Open the LR bilty, which lists the recorded mileage at pickup, and compare it to the current reading.</li>
      <li>Calculate the distance traveled and verify it aligns with the scheduled route and expected usage.</li>
      <li>Record the verified mileage in the delivery log, noting any deviations and the reason (e.g., detours, maintenance).</li>
    </ul>
  </li>

  <li><strong>Signed Condition Sign‑Off</strong>
    <ul>
      <li>Both the delivery agent and the recipient sign a condition sheet that lists all inspected points and confirms the odometer match.</li>
      <li>The sheet must include the date, time, and location of handover, as well as the names and signatures of all parties.</li>
      <li>Attach any photographic evidence of discrepancies and the signed condition sheet to the final delivery report.</li>
      <li>Submit the completed report to the logistics manager within 24 hours of delivery, ensuring traceability and accountability.</li>
    </ul>
  </li>
</ul>

<p>By following this structured handover, the transport team ensures that every motorcycle arrives in the expected condition, with mileage accurately recorded, and all parties have acknowledged the vehicle’s status. This reduces disputes, protects the company’s reputation, and provides a clear audit trail for future reference.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>



